(1⁷) (Deleted by the Law of 28.04.2022)

(2) A credit institution that provides investment services or ancillary services must meet and observe the following requirements:
1) establish units for the provision of investment services and ancillary services and ensure the management, internal supervision and review, and audit of those units, including laying down the procedure by which employees of those units may receive investment services from that unit and from another credit institution or investment firm;
2) ensure that the head of that unit is a person competent in investment matters and of impeccable reputation;
3) ensure the execution of transactions in financial instruments, and the confidentiality of clients' financial instrument accounts and transactions, in accordance with the requirements of the law;
4) take security measures for the processing, storage and transmission of data in accordance with the requirements of this Law, the regulations of Latvijas Banka and its internal rules;
5) keep the financial instruments of clients and of the credit institution itself separate at all times;
6) retain the supporting documents for transactions in financial instruments and for the other services provided and transactions carried out for five years, and meet the other requirements laid down in the regulations of Latvijas Banka and in Regulation 2017/565 on completing and retaining supporting documents. Latvijas Banka may extend the period laid down in this Clause to up to seven years;
7) ensure that the requirements for retaining supporting documents are also observed in respect of records of telephone conversations or electronic communications, at least in relation to transactions concluded when dealing on own account and to the provision of services relating to the reception, transmission and execution of client orders. Such telephone conversations and electronic communications also include those intended to result in transactions concluded when dealing on own account or in the provision of services relating to the reception, transmission and execution of client orders, even if those conversations and communications do not result in the conclusion of such transactions. In order to ensure that the requirements for retaining supporting documents are met in respect of records of telephone conversations or electronic communications, the credit institution must:
a) take all reasonable steps to record relevant telephone conversations and electronic communications made, sent or received using equipment provided by the credit institution to an employee or contractor, or the use of which by an employee or contractor has been accepted or permitted by the credit institution,
b) notify clients that telephone conversations or communications between the credit institution and its clients that result or may result in transactions will be recorded. Such a notification may be made once, before the provision of investment services to clients,
c) not provide investment services and activities by telephone to clients who have not been notified in advance of the recording of telephone conversations or communications, where such investment services and activities relate to the reception, transmission and execution of client orders,
d) be able to accept client orders through other channels, provided that such communications are made in a durable form. The relevant face-to-face conversation with a client may be recorded by means of written minutes or notes. Such orders are regarded as equivalent to orders received by telephone,
e) take all reasonable steps to prevent an employee or contractor from making, sending or receiving relevant telephone calls and electronic communications on private equipment, thereby preventing the investment firm from recording or copying them;
8) ensure the continuous and systematic provision of investment services and ancillary services, using appropriate systems, resources and procedures;
9) take all necessary administrative and organisational measures to prevent the conflicts of interest referred to in Section 127 of this Law from adversely affecting the interests of clients;
10) establish sound security mechanisms to guarantee the security and authentication of the means of transfer of information, to minimise the risk of data corruption and unauthorised access and to prevent information leakage, maintaining the confidentiality of the data at all times.

(2¹) Additional requirements for the provision of investment services are laid down in Regulation No 2017/565.

(3) (Deleted by the Law of 21.06.2018)

(4) (Deleted by the Law of 21.06.2018)

