(1) Under a consumer credit agreement, a person engaged in consumer lending (hereinafter 'the creditor') grants or promises to grant a consumer credit in the form of a deferred payment, a loan or another similar financial accommodation. A contract for the provision of continuing services, digital content or digital services, or for the supply of goods, is not regarded as a consumer credit agreement within the meaning of this Law where the consumer pays for the goods or services, digital content or digital services in instalments during the term of the contract.

(1¹) Lending services may be provided to consumers by a company that has received a special permit (licence) to provide consumer lending services [hereinafter 'the special permit (licence)'] and whose minimum share capital to be paid up is EUR 425 000. These requirements do not apply to:
1) a company that is regarded as a credit institution under the laws and regulations governing the activities of credit institutions;
2) a manufacturer, seller or service provider that offers payment for the purchase of goods, services, digital content or digital services in the form of a deferred payment, a loan or another similar financial accommodation without involving financing from a third party;
3) a trader who, under a contract concluded between a manufacturer, seller or service provider, offers for the purchase of goods, services, digital content or digital services only consumer credit agreements under which no interest or other additional charges are payable;
4) a savings and loan association;
5) an administrator under the Segto obligāciju likums;
6) a securitisation company and a servicer, where the servicer is the originator which, before the assets were transferred to the securitisation company, met Clause 1, 2, 3 or 4 of this Paragraph;
7) (Clause enters into force on 20.11.2026 and is included in the wording of the Law as of 20.11.2026. See Clause 47 of the Transitional Provisions);
8) another financial service provider not referred to in Clauses 1, 2, 4, 5 and 6 of this Paragraph whose activities have been authorised by Latvijas Banka and which is entitled by other laws and regulations to provide consumer lending services.

(1²) (Deleted by the Law of 17.09.2026)

(1³) The special permit (licence) is issued for an indefinite period. Ministru kabinets lays down the procedure for issuing, cancelling and suspending the special permit (licence), the requirements that a company must meet in order to receive the special permit (licence), including requirements on share capital and requirements concerning the members of the supervisory board and the management board of the company, the amount of the state fee for issuing the special permit (licence), and the amount of the annual state fee for supervising the activities of a provider of lending services and the procedure for paying it.

(1⁴) Consumer lending services also include services under which a consumer's item is accepted from the consumer for sale or safekeeping and payment for the item is made when the item is handed over, where the contract gives the consumer the right to withdraw from the contract against a charge.

