(5) In order to assess, in accordance with Paragraph 4.⁴ of this Section, a consumer's ability to repay the credit or a guarantor's ability to meet the obligations arising from a contract of guarantee, a creditor has the right to request and, through a credit information bureau, to receive in accordance with the procedure laid down in laws and regulations:
1) a statement from the Valsts ieņēmumu dienests on the income of the consumer or guarantor;
2) the information held by the Valsts sociālās apdrošināšanas aģentūra on pensions, benefits and allowances paid to the consumer or guarantor;
3) information from the Fizisko personu reģistrs on the date of birth of the consumer or guarantor and on any restrictions on their legal capacity.

(6) (Deleted by the Law of 19.06.2008)

(7) (Deleted by the Law of 28.10.2010)

(8) Ministru kabinets lays down the content of the statement on a borrower's income issued by the Valsts ieņēmumu dienests and the procedure for requesting and issuing the statement.

(8¹) Ministru kabinets lays down the content and scope of the information of the Valsts sociālās apdrošināšanas aģentūra referred to in Clause 2 of Paragraph 5 of this Section on pensions, benefits and allowances paid to the consumer or guarantor, the period covered by the information, the procedure for requesting and issuing it, and the amount of the service charge and the procedure for paying it.

(9) Paragraph 5 of this Section does not apply to lending for transactions carried out in financial instruments.

(10) A credit whose amount is equal to or greater than 100 minimum monthly wages may be granted:
1) for no more than 90 per cent of the market value of the immovable property concerned, where repayment is secured by a mortgage on immovable property;
2) for no more than 95 per cent of the purchase price of the immovable property concerned or of the planned construction costs, where repayment is secured by a mortgage on immovable property and a state guarantee in accordance with the state assistance for the purchase or construction of a dwelling provided for in the Law "Par palīdzību dzīvokļa jautājumu risināšanā".

(10¹) For consumer credit agreements financing the purchase of specific goods for an amount exceeding EUR 1400, credit may be granted for no more than 90 per cent of the price of the goods concerned. This Paragraph does not apply to consumer credit agreements for a credit whose repayment is secured by a mortgage on immovable property.

(11) Paragraphs 5 and 10 of this Section do not apply to consumer credit agreements concluded with residents of other countries, where the purpose of the credit is not the purchase or use of immovable property or of other property registrable in the public registers of the Republic of Latvia.

(12) Where a credit agreement has been concluded on the conclusion of which the consumer must place an item in the creditor's custody as security and under which the consumer's liability is limited to the pledged item alone, the creditor acquires the right to realise the unredeemed pledge to discharge the consumer's credit obligations on the seventh day after the end of the repayment term stated in the credit agreement.

(13) Where the pledge referred to in Paragraph 12 of this Section is not redeemed by the end of the repayment term stated in the credit agreement, the consumer has the right to redeem it until the creditor realises that item to discharge the consumer's debt obligations. The charge for the use of the credit or the administrative expenses (where provided for in the credit agreement concluded by the parties) demanded for redeeming the pledge after the end of the redemption period laid down in the credit agreement must not exceed the charges or expenses applied during the term of the credit agreement.

(14) After the sale of the pledged item referred to in Paragraph 13 of this Section, the creditor's right of claim against the consumer is extinguished even where the proceeds from the realisation of the item are not sufficient to cover the consumer's credit obligations.

(15) When developing consumer lending services, advertising lending services, granting credit, providing credit intermediation services, giving advice, providing ancillary services in connection with lending services to consumers or performing the obligations under a credit agreement, a creditor, a credit intermediary or an appointed representative of a credit intermediary must act honestly, fairly, transparently and professionally, taking into account the rights and interests of the consumer. In the laws and regulations governing consumer lending, giving advice means providing personal recommendations to a consumer in respect of one or more transactions related to a credit agreement, as an activity separate from the granting of credit and from credit intermediation.

(16) Authorities must, within their competence and the budget funds allocated, and in cooperation with consumer protection associations, promote consumer education in the field of consumer lending, in particular on responsible borrowing and debt management.

