(1) A financial institution referred to in Section 71 of this Law must provide the Valsts ieņēmumu dienests with the following information on each reportable account that the financial institution identifies in accordance with the due diligence procedures for accounts laid down by Ministru kabinets:
1) where the account holder is a natural person: the given name, surname, date and place of birth and address of the participating jurisdiction person who is the account holder, the name of the participating jurisdiction concerned, the taxpayer identification number (where one is issued) and an indication of whether the account holder has submitted a reliable self-certification of tax residence;
2) where the account holder is a legal arrangement: the name and address of the participating jurisdiction person who is the account holder, the name of the participating jurisdiction concerned, the taxpayer identification number (where one is issued) and an indication of whether the account holder has submitted a reliable self-certification of tax residence;
3) where the account holder is a legal arrangement that has one or more beneficial owners who, after the application of the due diligence procedures, have been identified as reportable persons: the name and address of the account holder, information on its status as a tax resident of the participating jurisdiction and of another country, its taxpayer identification number (where one is issued), and for each beneficial owner who is a reportable participating jurisdiction person, the given name, surname, date and place of birth, the status of the reportable person (where the person is a beneficial owner of the legal arrangement), the address, the name of the participating jurisdiction concerned and the taxpayer identification number (where one is issued), as well as an indication of whether a reliable self-certification of tax residence has been submitted for each reportable person;
3¹) an indication of whether the reportable account is a jointly held account, also stating the number of account holders;
4) the account number (or functional equivalent in the absence of an account number), the type of account and an indication of whether it is a new account or a preexisting account;
5) the name and identifying number (if any) of the reporting financial institution;
6) the account balance or value (including, in the case of a cash value insurance contract or an annuity contract, the cash value or surrender value) as of the end of the relevant calendar year or other appropriate reporting period or, if the account was closed during that year or period, information on the closure of the account;
7) in the case of a custodial account:
a) the total gross amount of interest, the total gross amount of dividends and the total gross amount of other income generated with respect to the assets held in the account, in each case paid or credited to the account (or with respect to the account) during the calendar year or other appropriate reporting period,
b) the total gross proceeds from the sale or redemption of financial assets paid or credited to the account during the calendar year or other appropriate reporting period with respect to which the reporting financial institution acted as a custodial institution, an investment entity, a nominee holder of financial assets or an agent of the account holder;
8) in the case of a depository account: the total gross amount of interest paid or credited to the account during the calendar year or other appropriate reporting period;
8¹) the status under which the reportable person holds an equity interest, where that equity interest is held in an investment entity established on a contractual basis;
9) in the case of any reportable financial account other than those referred to in Clause 7 or 8 of this Paragraph: the total gross amount paid or credited to the account holder with respect to the account (including the aggregate amount of any redemption payments made to the account holder) during the calendar year or other appropriate reporting period with respect to which the reporting financial institution is the obligor or debtor.

(2) The information reported in accordance with Paragraph 1 of this Section must state the currency in which each amount is denominated.

(3) Where a reportable account is a preexisting account, a financial institution, notwithstanding Clauses 1, 2 and 3 of Paragraph 1 of this Section, is not required to report the taxpayer identification number or date of birth of the account holder or beneficial owner where that taxpayer identification number or date of birth is not in the financial institution's records. The reporting financial institution must take the additional steps necessary to obtain the taxpayer identification number or date of birth with respect to preexisting accounts by the end of the second calendar year following the year in which the preexisting accounts were identified as reportable accounts, and whenever, in the course of applying the customer identification and due diligence procedures approved by the financial institution in accordance with the Noziedzīgi iegūtu līdzekļu legalizācijas un terorisma un proliferācijas finansēšanas novēršanas likums, it needs to update the information on a preexisting account.

(4) Notwithstanding Clauses 1 and 3 of Paragraph 1 of this Section, the place of birth need not be reported unless:
1) the reporting financial institution has been required to obtain and report it under other laws and regulations;
2) it is available in the electronically searchable data maintained by the reporting financial institution.

(4¹) Notwithstanding Sub-clause "b" of Clause 7 of Paragraph 1 of this Section, and unless the reporting financial institution elects otherwise with respect to any clearly identified group of accounts, the gross proceeds from the sale or redemption of financial assets need not be reported to the extent that the reporting financial institution reports such gross proceeds from the sale or redemption of those financial assets in accordance with Section 15, Paragraph 12 of this Law.

(5) Ministru kabinets lays down the procedure by which financial institutions provide the information referred to in Paragraph 1 of this Section to the Valsts ieņēmumu dienests for transmission to the competent authority of another country, and by which the Valsts ieņēmumu dienests transmits that information to the competent authorities of other countries.

(6) Before submitting reports to the Valsts ieņēmumu dienests, a reporting financial institution must inform its customers on whom a report is to be submitted that their data will be processed and transmitted to the Valsts ieņēmumu dienests in accordance with the procedure laid down in this Chapter and for the intended purpose.

(As amended by the Laws of 20.02.2020 and 06.11.2025, which enter into force on 01.01.2026. See Clause 251 of the Transitional Provisions)

texts.lv:
(1) Šā likuma 55. panta pirmās daļas 6. un 7. punktā minēto pārmeklēšanas un apskates darbību laikā pēc Latvijas Bankas likumīga pieprasījuma Latvijas Bankas uzraudzītajam finanšu tirgus dalībniekam, tā amatpersonai un darbiniekam, kā arī citai personai, ja ir pamats uzskatīt, ka šī persona ir saistīta ar tiesību aktu iespējamu pārkāpumu vai ka tās rīcībā varētu būt pārkāpuma apstākļu noskaidrošanai nepieciešamā informācija Latvijas Bankas ierosinātajā administratīvajā lietā, ir pienākums:
1) nodrošināt piekļuvi jebkuriem to īpašumā, valdījumā vai lietošanā esošajiem pārmeklējamiem objektiem, atverot tos un tajos esošās glabātavas;
2) nodrošināt piekļuvi jebkurā veidā un formā sagatavotam vai uzglabātam dokumentam, kā arī elektroniskajā informācijas sistēmā saglabātajām ziņām (datiem);
3) Latvijas Bankas noteiktajā termiņā sniegt pilnīgu un patiesu pieprasīto informāciju;
4) izsniegt pieprasīto dokumentu vai tā atvasinājumu;
5) apliecināt elektroniskajā informācijas sistēmā saglabāto ziņu (datu) izdruku vai elektroniskajos informācijas nesējos izdarīto ierakstu autentiskumu;
6) izpildīt citas Latvijas Bankas padomes locekļa, darbinieka un pilnvarnieka likumīgās prasības.

(2) Par šā panta pirmajā daļā minēto pienākumu nepildīšanu Latvijas Banka piemēro sankciju — soda naudu fiziskajai personai līdz 700 euro, bet juridiskajai personai — no 1400 līdz 15 000 euro.

(3) Administratīvo lietu var ierosināt ne vēlāk kā mēneša laikā no pārkāpuma izdarīšanas dienas.

(4) Pieņemot lēmumu par šā panta otrajā daļā minēto sankciju piemērošanu, Latvijas Banka ņem vērā šā likuma 62. panta trešās daļas 3., 6. un 8. punktā minētos kritērijus, kā arī personas iepriekš izdarītos pārkāpumus šā panta pirmajā daļā noteikto Latvijas Bankas veikto pārmeklēšanas un apskates darbību izpildes laikā.

(5) Sankcija piemērojama ne vēlāk kā sešu mēnešu laikā pēc administratīvās lietas ierosināšanas dienas. Soda nauda ieskaitāma valsts pamatbudžetā.

(6) Sankcijas piemērošana neatbrīvo no tā pienākuma izpildīšanas, par kura nepildīšanu piemērota sankcija.

(Ar grozījumiem, kas izdarīti ar 14.05.2026. likumu, kas stājas spēkā 09.06.2026.)

texts.en:
(1) During the search and inspection activities referred to in Clauses 6 and 7 of Section 55, Paragraph 1 of this Law, a financial market participant supervised by Latvijas Banka, its officials and employees, and any other person where there are grounds to believe that the person is connected with a possible breach of legal acts or may hold information necessary to establish the circumstances of the breach in administrative proceedings initiated by Latvijas Banka, must, at the lawful request of Latvijas Banka:
1) provide access to any premises to be searched that they own, possess or use, by opening them and the storage places within them;
2) provide access to any document prepared or stored in any way and form, and to information (data) stored in an electronic information system;
3) provide the requested information, complete and true, within the time limit set by Latvijas Banka;
4) hand over the requested document or a derivative of it;
5) certify the authenticity of printouts of information (data) stored in an electronic information system or of records made on electronic data carriers;
6) comply with the other lawful demands of a member of the Council, an employee or an authorised representative of Latvijas Banka.

(2) For failure to fulfil the obligations referred to in Paragraph 1 of this Section, Latvijas Banka imposes a sanction consisting of a fine of up to EUR 700 on a natural person, and of EUR 1400 to EUR 15 000 on a legal person.

(3) Administrative proceedings may be initiated no later than one month from the day on which the breach was committed.

(4) When deciding to impose the sanctions referred to in Paragraph 2 of this Section, Latvijas Banka takes into account the criteria referred to in Clauses 3, 6 and 8 of Section 62, Paragraph 3 of this Law, as well as previous breaches committed by the person during the search and inspection activities carried out by Latvijas Banka referred to in Paragraph 1 of this Section.

(5) The sanction must be imposed no later than six months after the day on which the administrative proceedings were initiated. Fines are paid into the state basic budget.

(6) The imposition of a sanction does not release the person from fulfilling the obligation whose non-fulfilment led to the sanction.

(As amended by the Law of 14.05.2026, which enters into force on 09.06.2026)

